  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Regional Refugee and Migrant Response Plan (RMRP) 2023 - 2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ongoing political and socio-economic developments in the Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela have led to the outflow of millions of Venezuelans into neighboring countries and beyond. The Latin America and Caribbean (LAC) region has never experienced, in modern history, such a large-scale movement of both migrants and refugees. In the last six years, this number has grown nearly ten times as large, to approximately 7.3 million migrants and refugees from Venezuela outside their country worldwide, with more than 6 million hosted in LAC as of January 2023. As part of the ongoing response under the Regional Refugee and Migrant Response Plan for Refugees and Migrants from Venezuela (RMRP) 2023-2024, in 2023 over 3,410,000 million Venezuelans are currently directly targeted through the coordinated actions of the Interagency Coordination Platform for Refugees and Migrants (R4V) partners. Through this allocation from the Government of Norway towards the RMRP 2023-2024, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) is contributing to the mitigation of humanitarian needs of migrants, refugees and community members affected by the mixed migration flows from Venezuela in LAC. This allocation will be dedicated to IOM activities in Aruba, Costa Rica, Curacao and Panama.</narrative>
  </description>
